\title{Words by length}
\date{2026-03-04T03:00:35Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{Under the [equivalence relation #{L}](0091) (words are related if they have the same length), the [equivalence class](0097) of “dog” is the set of all three-letter English words: ##{[\text{dog}] = \{ \text{dog}, \text{cow},
    \text{hat}, \text{eat}, \dots \}.} This is a finite (but large) set.}

